<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Vista Butte from Vista Butte Sno-Park</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:273-1b: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.983802" lon="-121.606363"><ele>1802.1</ele><name>Vista Butte Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead th:vista-butte-sno-park (Google place; ODOT 43.9840, -121.6063); confidence: high; pdf_page: 275; quote: The most direct route is from the Vista Butte Sno-Park ... Ski up the trail from the sno-park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.985996" lon="-121.612579"><ele>1845.1</ele><name>Trail turns uphill</name><desc>source: OSM: nordic way/878847274 (passes 10 m from the pin, runs west above the highway) meets track way/878964266 and nordic way/878964264 at node/38267940; confidence: low; pdf_page: 276; quote: At 0.4 mile it makes a turn, and in 0.2 mile the trail forks (map 62: 0.6 west from the sno-park, then a 0.6 steep leg and a 0.9 leg)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.986820" lon="-121.610218"><ele>1843.6</ele><name>Junction below the Butte Trail</name><desc>source: OSM: nordic ways 878964264 and 878847273 and track way/5354278 meet; confidence: low; pdf_page: 276; quote: Both of these short legs (0.6 and 0.9 mile) join above</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.989552" lon="-121.607678"><ele>1873.6</ele><name>Butte Trail</name><desc>source: OSM: nordic way/878847273 meets Swampy-Dutchman Trail #40 (Butte Trail); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 276; quote: the trail continues 1 mile to Bruce's Ball Park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.993590" lon="-121.603570"><ele>1938.1</ele><name>Bruce's Ball Park</name><desc>source: OSM: Vista Butte Trail #40.2 (way 299952087) leaves the Butte Trail; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 276; quote: where the trail to the summit of the butte goes to the right</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.992055" lon="-121.598381"><ele>2016.1</ele><name>Vista Butte summit</name><desc>source: OSM node 3040323668 Vista Butte; confidence: high; pdf_page: 275; book_elev_ft: 6619; quote: The summit of the 6,619-foot butte ... is a wide, windy snow ridge</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Vista Butte from Vista Butte Sno-Park</name><desc>1. Vista Butte Sno-Park -&gt; Trail turns uphill: osm (medium), 0.98 mi | 2. Trail turns uphill -&gt; Junction below the Butte Trail: osm (low), 0.16 mi | 3. Junction below the Butte Trail -&gt; Butte Trail: osm (medium), 0.54 mi | 4. Butte Trail -&gt; Bruce's Ball Park: osm (high), 0.49 mi | 5. Bruce's Ball Park -&gt; Vista Butte summit: osm (high), 0.50 mi</desc>
